From: "Baptiste G." <70719480+BeeeFX@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Node graph: the drawing of nodes and links as preferences

The node graph drew its nodes and links with sizes and colours written in the code (NODE_WIDTH and
NODE_HEIGHT, a 5 px corner radius, Natron's shading, a 3 px black link pen with 14 px, 24 degree arrow
heads, a white link when selected, a light yellow halo around a selected node, a thin black cross on a
disabled node, 15 px Dots, a postage stamp on every new Read node). Each is now a preference in
Appearance > Node Graph > Node and link drawing, and every default is the value the code had, so nothing
changes for anyone who doesn't set them:

  nodeTileWidth, nodeTileHeight, nodeCornerRadius, nodeShading, nodeOutlineColor, nodeSelectedColor,
  nodeSelectedTint (a selected node takes the selection colour instead of the halo; backdrops keep the
  halo), dotDiameter, linkWidth (the line drawn; the item's pen keeps 3 px for picking), linkColor,
  linkSelectedColor, linkArrowLength, linkArrowAngle, disabledCrossColor, disabledCrossWidth,
  readerPreview (whether a new Read node shows its postage stamp).

Values are read when a node is made and when a link is drawn, so a script can set them for a session
(the BeeeFX fork's layer sets Nuke-like values) without touching anyone's stored preferences.

Core patch 0001 of the BeeeFX fork (layer/patches/), written to be offered upstream as it is.

Also (second commit on sng/main): A new preference, nodeFitLabel (Appearance > Node Graph > Node and link drawing, off by default: every node
keeps the same width, as before), lets a node whose label is longer than the node width grow to fit it. The
width is measured from the node's initial width plus the label, never from its current width, so it can't
creep (the reason the width was left alone); backdrops and nodes showing a postage stamp size themselves as
before. Read by name from the settings, so Settings.h doesn't change.

Gap: layer/GAPS.md, "Nuke's look and habits" (the node graph's drawing).
Size: 9 files changed, 255 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-).
upstream: not offered yet (to offer to Niik-l: github.com/Niik-l/Natron).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
